IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-rate`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-rate (regs 77.7 and 77.93). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1444-1457 and 1497-1510), beside each assertion, before the run. The earnings figures are invented for the tests.

§ `Purposes (src:1444, 1497)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.7(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 11` EQUALS "testing whether paying benefits based on calculating the rate of weekly benefits using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work"
#ASSERT `reg 77.93(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 16` EQUALS "testing whether paying benefits based on a rate of weekly benefits calculated using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work"

§ `Reg 77.7(2) - who is included in Pilot Project No. 11 (src:1445)`

-- The argument order is: the day the benefit period is established; resident in a region of Schedule II.8; the Fishing Regulations apply.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2008 10 26) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2011 6 25) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2008 10 25) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2011 6 26) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2010 1 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- A claimant to whom the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE)

§ `Reg 77.93(2) - who is included in Pilot Project No. 16 (src:1498)`

-- The argument order is: the day the benefit period is established; resident in a region of Schedule II.91; Part VII.1 of the Act applies; the Fishing Regulations apply.
#ASSERT `reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2011 6 26) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2013 4 6) TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2011 6 25) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2013 4 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2012 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Part VII.1 of the Act applies (a self-employed person): excluded. So are Fishing Regulations claimants.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2012 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` (YMD 2012 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `Reg 77.7(3)(a) to (d), 77.93(3)(a) to (d) (src:1447-1450, 1500-1503)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(a), (d) and reg 77.93(3)(a), (d) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act and section 24.2 of the Regulations do not apply` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.7(3)(a), (d) and reg 77.93(3)(a), (d) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act and section 24.2 of the Regulations do not apply` FALSE)
-- The argument order is: included; the rate calculation period (January 5 to March 29, 2009); the qualifying period (March 30, 2008 to March 28, 2009).
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(b), (c) and reg 77.93(3)(b), (c) the period that the reference to the rate calculation period reads as` TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 5), (YMD 2009 3 29)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 3 30), (YMD 2009 3 28)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 3 30), (YMD 2009 3 28)
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(b), (c) and reg 77.93(3)(b), (c) the period that the reference to the rate calculation period reads as` FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 5), (YMD 2009 3 29)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 3 30), (YMD 2009 3 28)) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 5), (YMD 2009 3 29)

§ `Reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and 77.93(3)(e), (f) - the weekly insurable earnings (src:1451-1454, 1504-1507)`

-- Twenty weeks: ten of 700, four of 350, six of 100. The 14 highest are the ten of 700 and the four of 350: 7000 + 1400 = 8400, and 8400 divided by 14 is 600.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` (LIST 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 100, 700) 0 EQUALS 600
-- The same weeks with 1,400 paid or payable under section 24.1: (8400 + 1400) / 14 = 700.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` (LIST 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 350, 700, 100, 700, 100, 700) 1400 EQUALS 700
-- Exactly 14 weeks of 500: 7000 / 14 = 500.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` (LIST 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500, 500) 0 EQUALS 500
-- Ten weeks only, of 700: the text says divide by 14, so 7000 / 14 = 500 (the reading taken, fork F-reg77.7e).
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` (LIST 700, 700, 700, 700, 700, 700, 700, 700, 700, 700) 0 EQUALS 500

§ `Reg 77.7(4) and 77.93(4) - earnings reported by pay period (src:1455-1457, 1508-1510)`

-- (a): 1,400 reported for a two-week pay period of 14 days; a full week of 7 days takes half: 700.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` 1400 14 7 EQUALS JUST 700
-- A monthly pay period of 31 days with 3,100 reported: a full week takes 7/31, which is 700; a week with 3 of its days in the pay period takes 3/31, which is 300.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` 3100 31 7 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` 3100 31 3 EQUALS JUST 300
-- A pay period of no days cannot be shared.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` 3100 0 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): 1,400 reported for 14 days; evidence that one week (7 days) actually earned 500; the other week takes (1400 - 500) x 7 / (14 - 7) = 900.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(b) and reg 77.93(4)(b) the insurable earnings allocated to one of the other weeks` 1400 14 7 (LIST 500) 7 EQUALS JUST 900
-- A monthly pay period: 3,100 reported over 31 days; one week of 7 days evidenced at 1,000; another full week takes (3100 - 1000) x 7 / (31 - 7) = 612.5.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(b) and reg 77.93(4)(b) the insurable earnings allocated to one of the other weeks` 3100 31 7 (LIST 1000) 7 EQUALS JUST 612.5
-- Every week of the pay period evidenced: there is no other week.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4)(b) and reg 77.93(4)(b) the insurable earnings allocated to one of the other weeks` 1400 14 7 (LIST 500, 900) 14 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.7(4) and 77.93(4) as a whole (src:1455-1457, 1508-1510)`

-- The argument order is: the earnings reported for the pay period; its days; the days of the week in it; evidence of the amount actually earned in a week is provided; the evidenced amounts; the days of those weeks.
-- Without evidence, (a): 1,400 over a pay period of 14 days; a week of 7 days takes 700.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4) and reg 77.93(4) the insurable earnings allocated to a week with no evidence of its own` 1400 14 7 FALSE EMPTY 0 EQUALS JUST 700
-- With evidence of 500 for one week of 7 days, (b): the other week takes 900.
#ASSERT `reg 77.7(4) and reg 77.93(4) the insurable earnings allocated to a week with no evidence of its own` 1400 14 7 TRUE (LIST 500) 7 EQUALS JUST 900
